nodecode-colab is a rewrite of PietrangeloManco's PietrangeloManco/hermes-colab:
https://github.com/PietrangeloManco/hermes-colab
commit f05cf934fff3b446f2e00cc32e19432e9e41e87b
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Pietrangelo Manco (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's eight tools became seven Nodecode tools and
a /colab command (colab_resume folded into the run, which resumes by
itself). The Colab tunnel endpoints, the assignment dance, the keep-alive,
the unassign, the runtime proxy token, the Jupyter kernel, the outputs that
come home and the fresh runtime after a reclaim are the same protocol,
reimplemented against NLK:HTTP and websocket-driver. What was left out and
why: the Hermes OAuth store and the dashboard page, which have no Nodecode
counterpart here, so the Google grant is read from the cell's own section;
the SQLite run store, since a run lives in the cell's memory with its log
and outputs on disk; and the zip bundle, papermill notebooks, detached
runner and pre_llm_call notice, which this executes in the kernel and
reports with nle:notice instead.
